3195
01:59:30.425 --> 01:59:33.714
this process is essentially anathema

3196
01:59:33.714 --> 01:59:35.282
it's counterintuitive path

3197
01:59:35.282 --> 01:59:37.449
that is just off the table

3198
01:59:38.584 --> 01:59:41.334
rather than remain stuck in pain.

3199
01:59:44.546 --> 01:59:46.051
I think many people are,

3200
01:59:46.051 --> 01:59:47.864
what am I trying to say?

3201
01:59:47.864 --> 01:59:49.327
I think there are a lot of people

3202
01:59:49.327 --> 01:59:51.262
who would rather remain stuck in pain

3203
01:59:51.262 --> 01:59:52.595
than appear weak

3204
01:59:53.488 --> 01:59:55.076
because showing your truth

3205
01:59:55.076 --> 01:59:57.493
is a very terrifying prospect

3206
01:59:58.525 --> 02:00:01.551
I think particularly for a lot of men.

3207
02:00:01.551 --> 02:00:03.220
And so over the years,

3208
02:00:03.220 --> 02:00:05.380
I've worked hard to dispel this myth,

3209
02:00:05.380 --> 02:00:06.930
that vulnerability is weakness

3210
02:00:06.930 --> 02:00:08.784
that showing emotion is weakness.

3211
02:00:08.784 --> 02:00:09.914
And that by leading

3212
02:00:09.914 --> 02:00:12.497
with vulnerability and emotion,

3213
02:00:14.095 --> 02:00:16.646
it's like this disarming force

3214
02:00:16.646 --> 02:00:18.471
that allows and permits others

3215
02:00:18.471 --> 02:00:21.221
to kind of meet me in that space.

3216
02:00:23.393 --> 02:00:24.723
And I think it's also correct

3217
02:00:24.723 --> 02:00:26.808
that most men, young boys

3218
02:00:26.808 --> 02:00:28.809
adolescents suffer in silence,

3219
02:00:28.809 --> 02:00:30.497
their emotions are in lock down.

3220
02:00:30.497 --> 02:00:32.931
They're afraid of being open and honest with anybody.

3221
02:00:32.931 --> 02:00:35.449
And over time, if not unlocked,

3222
02:00:35.449 --> 02:00:36.575
like this is gonna fester,

3223
02:00:36.575 --> 02:00:38.061
it's going to metastasize

3224
02:00:38.061 --> 02:00:39.880
and the result is never good.

3225
02:00:39.880 --> 02:00:40.937
And that's when we get

3226
02:00:40.937 --> 02:00:44.386
into toxic masculinity and violence.

3227
02:00:44.386 --> 02:00:47.315
So it's about normalizing the process

3228
02:00:47.315 --> 02:00:49.019
of asking and receiving help.

3229
02:00:49.019 --> 02:00:53.911
It's about normalizing vulnerability and understanding

3230
02:00:53.911 --> 02:00:57.764
that vulnerability and being kind of more

3231
02:00:57.764 --> 02:01:00.069
on the surface with your emotions

3232
02:01:00.069 --> 02:01:03.223
is not mutually exclusive from masculinity.

3233
02:01:03.223 --> 02:01:05.076
You can love football,

3234
02:01:05.076 --> 02:01:07.163
you can love MMA and cars and guns

3235
02:01:07.163 --> 02:01:10.442
or whatever we associate with conventional norms

3236
02:01:10.442 --> 02:01:12.316
that surround our definition of what is

3237
02:01:12.316 --> 02:01:13.780
and what isn't masculine

3238
02:01:13.780 --> 02:01:16.363
and be open honest, vulnerable,

3239
02:01:17.220 --> 02:01:19.553
caring, all of those things.

3240
02:01:20.822 --> 02:01:22.322
And inquisitive.

3241
02:01:23.639 --> 02:01:26.472
I think that you demonstrate that.

3242
02:01:27.878 --> 02:01:30.919
I think that's part of the appeal to David Goggins

3243
02:01:30.919 --> 02:01:33.193
the major part of it, and Joe Rogan as well,

3244
02:01:33.193 --> 02:01:35.366
kind of like this masculine version

3245
02:01:35.366 --> 02:01:36.991
of being open inquisitive

3246
02:01:36.991 --> 02:01:40.543
and vulnerable about life basically.

3247
02:01:40.543 --> 02:01:43.378
I think the podcast host

3248
02:01:43.378 --> 02:01:45.708
that exemplifies it perhaps better

3249
02:01:45.708 --> 02:01:47.492
than anybody is Dax Shepard,

3250
02:01:47.492 --> 02:01:49.868
because he's very much like a dudes dude.

3251
02:01:49.868 --> 02:01:50.834
He likes to race cars

3252
02:01:50.834 --> 02:01:53.818
and he wears like cutoff shirts

3253
02:01:53.818 --> 02:01:55.057
and he's a blue collar guy

3254
02:01:55.057 --> 02:01:57.450
from Michigan and like chews tobacco.

3255
02:01:57.450 --> 02:01:59.272
And he's a dudes dude

3256
02:01:59.272 --> 02:02:01.184
but he's also somebody

3257
02:02:01.184 --> 02:02:03.055
who wears his emotions on his sleeve

3258
02:02:03.055 --> 02:02:04.491
and he's very vulnerable.

3259
02:02:04.491 --> 02:02:06.884
And he tells his friends, he loves them.

3260
02:02:06.884 --> 02:02:08.109
He does all this stuff

3261
02:02:08.109 --> 02:02:09.509
that is sort of countered

3262
02:02:09.509 --> 02:02:11.742
to what you think like a dudes dude would do.

3263
02:02:11.742 --> 02:02:12.750
And I think it's part

3264
02:02:12.750 --> 02:02:16.161
of why his message is so powerful and impactful

3265
02:02:16.161 --> 02:02:19.196
and why I think he's such a good podcast host.

3266
02:02:19.196 --> 02:02:21.849
But it's that like combination,

3267
02:02:21.849 --> 02:02:24.872
like I'm not a dudes dude in the way

3268
02:02:24.872 --> 02:02:28.955
that Dax is but I still would characterize myself

3269
02:02:30.154 --> 02:02:32.341
as having a certain kind of masculinity

3270
02:02:32.341 --> 02:02:34.752
that through a lot of internal work

3271
02:02:34.752 --> 02:02:36.455
is not under threat

3272
02:02:36.455 --> 02:02:38.425
because I tell you, Adam, I love you.

3273
02:02:38.425 --> 02:02:39.258
You know what I mean?

3274
02:02:39.258 --> 02:02:40.376
Thank you. I love you too.

3275
02:02:40.376 --> 02:02:42.473
Yes, we'll make out afterwards.

3276
02:02:42.473 --> 02:02:43.306
I agree.

3277
02:02:44.251 --> 02:02:45.190
I mean, my story,

3278
02:02:45.190 --> 02:02:46.539
I'm gonna drop a little bomb here

3279
02:02:46.539 --> 02:02:48.327
but we don't have to belabor it too much,

3280
02:02:48.327 --> 02:02:49.410
but I grew up

3281
02:02:50.359 --> 02:02:53.391
I was sexually abused at seven years old.

3282
02:02:53.391 --> 02:02:54.594
I didn't know that.

3283
02:02:54.594 --> 02:02:56.894
And then grew up

3284
02:02:56.894 --> 02:02:59.600
and went through puberty late

3285
02:02:59.600 --> 02:03:03.933
and was really small for my age most of my life,

3286
02:03:03.933 --> 02:03:05.375
even though I was interested in sports

3287
02:03:05.375 --> 02:03:07.627
and was pretty good.

3288
02:03:07.627 --> 02:03:10.754
I had to question myself along the way

3289
02:03:10.754 --> 02:03:13.212
and I kind of like stuffed down the abuse

3290
02:03:13.212 --> 02:03:14.226
for a long time.

3291
02:03:14.226 --> 02:03:16.131
I didn't tell anybody.

3292
02:03:16.131 --> 02:03:17.808
And then I didn't really come up

3293
02:03:17.808 --> 02:03:20.558
and address it until what was it?

3294
02:03:21.975 --> 02:03:25.158
Like 99, 2000 I think right around there.

3295
02:03:25.158 --> 02:03:28.360
So I would be 28 around then,

3296
02:03:28.360 --> 02:03:30.249
is when I first started to deal with it.

3297
02:03:30.249 --> 02:03:32.931
And at first it was hard.

3298
02:03:32.931 --> 02:03:35.705
Guru Singh helped me through it at the beginning.

3299
02:03:35.705 --> 02:03:38.739
And I went through a process of therapy through him,

3300
02:03:38.739 --> 02:03:40.521
but not through traditional means

3301
02:03:40.521 --> 02:03:42.125
like going to a psychotherapist.

3302
02:03:42.125 --> 02:03:43.495
I went to a yoga teacher

3303
02:03:43.495 --> 02:03:46.216
who happens to be a great therapist also,

3304
02:03:46.216 --> 02:03:48.872
but he's not traditional.

3305
02:03:48.872 --> 02:03:53.083
And at the same time kind of like what's helped me.

3306
02:03:53.083 --> 02:03:54.757
Isn't been attaching to, I've never felt

3307
02:03:54.757 --> 02:03:56.789
like I needed to be some macho dude.

3308
02:03:56.789 --> 02:03:59.002
That's never been my thing 'cause I never was.

3309
02:03:59.002 --> 02:04:00.410
'Cause I was always kind of smaller

3310
02:04:00.410 --> 02:04:03.150
and felt smaller even when I grew.

3311
02:04:03.150 --> 02:04:05.557
And so I just never felt the need to do it.

3312
02:04:05.557 --> 02:04:08.307
I never wanted to be in that mode

3313
02:04:10.415 --> 02:04:11.931
and was never attracted to it.

3314
02:04:11.931 --> 02:04:13.681
But at the same time,

3315
02:04:14.787 --> 02:04:16.551
I'll bro out just like anybody else.

3316
02:04:16.551 --> 02:04:19.002
So I understand that like having a group

3317
02:04:19.002 --> 02:04:22.197
of guy friends can be empowering to young guys

3318
02:04:22.197 --> 02:04:25.490
and having some people you're close to you can be.

3319
02:04:25.490 --> 02:04:28.070
And so that was never a problem for me either.

3320
02:04:28.070 --> 02:04:28.903
So I've kind of

3321
02:04:28.903 --> 02:04:31.566
as riding this line of having the secret

3322
02:04:31.566 --> 02:04:35.032
and broing out and never really addressing it.

3323
02:04:35.032 --> 02:04:36.639
What's helped me most of all

3324
02:04:36.639 --> 02:04:39.304
has been kind of discovering things like yoga

3325
02:04:39.304 --> 02:04:41.585
which is kind of a more feminine practice

3326
02:04:41.585 --> 02:04:44.510
and Daoism which is a book I read

3327
02:04:44.510 --> 02:04:45.805
Taoism Ching from cover to cover.

3328
02:04:45.805 --> 02:04:47.940
Basically I read a verse,

3329
02:04:47.940 --> 02:04:49.669
maybe multiple days in a row,

3330
02:04:49.669 --> 02:04:51.200
then I'll start again at the beginning

3331
02:04:51.200 --> 02:04:52.763
and I'll switch translations.

3332
02:04:52.763 --> 02:04:54.457
And that is again, kind of looking

3333
02:04:54.457 --> 02:04:58.290
at the universe not in duality but in oneness.

3334
02:05:01.611 --> 02:05:03.379
I think my advice would be

3335
02:05:03.379 --> 02:05:05.828
or things I like to tell people is,

3336
02:05:05.828 --> 02:05:08.393
let's not try to look at things in duality.

3337
02:05:08.393 --> 02:05:10.404
Let's look at things as a unity

3338
02:05:10.404 --> 02:05:14.330
that we're a part of everything all the time.

3339
02:05:14.330 --> 02:05:16.696
And I'm not one of those people that's like

3340
02:05:16.696 --> 02:05:19.566
against gender constructs in any way shape or form.

3341
02:05:19.566 --> 02:05:21.188
I just think it's beyond gender.

3342
02:05:21.188 --> 02:05:22.791
It's a conversation beyond gender.

3343
02:05:22.791 --> 02:05:25.067
It's a connection beyond the individual.

3344
02:05:25.067 --> 02:05:28.217
It's an expansion that we are everything all the time.

3345
02:05:28.217 --> 02:05:31.098
And when you think of it, that way the deconcentration

3346
02:05:31.098 --> 02:05:33.931
of the small thing and get bigger.

3347
02:05:34.812 --> 02:05:39.125
Sometimes I feel like the luckiest man in the world.

3348
02:05:39.125 --> 02:05:41.682
I mean, well thank you for sharing that story.

3349
02:05:41.682 --> 02:05:43.121
I didn't know that about you.

3350
02:05:43.121 --> 02:05:43.954
Thanks.

3351
02:05:43.954 --> 02:05:45.071
That's pretty heavy.

3352
02:05:45.071 --> 02:05:46.226
